[ar:Simon & Garfunkel]
[al:Sounds of Silence]
[ti:The Sound of Silence]
[00:03.51] Hello darkness, my old friend
[00:07.66] I've come to talk with you again
[00:11.86] Because a vision softly creeping
[00:16.75] Left its seeds while I was sleeping
[00:21.31] And the vision that was planted in my brain
[00:27.67] Still remains
[00:30.82] Within the sound of silence
[00:37.09] In restless dreams, I walked alone
[00:41.93] Narrow streets of cobblestone
[00:46.12] 'Neath the halo of a streetlamp
[00:50.87] I turned my collar to the cold and damp
[00:55.59] When my eyes were stabbed by the flash of a neon light
[01:02.00] That split the night
[01:05.91] And touched the sound of silence
[01:11.32] And in the naked light, I saw
[01:15.73] Ten thousand people, maybe more
[01:20.50] People talking without speaking
[01:25.09] People hearing without listening
[01:29.36] People writing songs that voices never shared
[01:37.06] No one dared
[01:40.64] Disturb the sound of silence
[01:46.01] "Fools", said I, "You do not know
[01:50.67] Silence like a cancer grows
[01:54.91] Hear my words that I might teach you
[01:59.72] Take my arms that I might reach you"
[02:04.14] But my words like silent raindrops fell
[02:13.15] And echoed in the wells of silence
[02:20.51] And the people bowed and prayed
[02:25.05] To the neon god they made
[02:29.58] And the sign flashed out its warning
[02:33.63] In the words that it was forming
[02:38.47] And the sign said, "The words of the prophets are written on the subway walls
[02:45.65] In tenement halls"
[02:48.69] And whispered in the sounds of silence
[02:56.47] 
